TEXT 64 32 Left 2 ;I2C open-drain bus: pull-up and bus capacitance
TEXT 64 656 Left 2 !.model SWOD SW(Ron=0.1 Roff=1G Vt=2 Vh=0.1)\n.tran 0 40u 0 10n
TEXT 64 704 Left 2 ;Plot V(SDA). Released bus: tau = 4.7k x 200p = 0.94 us.
TEXT 64 768 Left 2 ;1. Click Run: the running-person button at the top left.
TEXT 64 808 Left 2 ;2. On the schematic, click the wire labeled SDA (not the component).
TEXT 64 848 Left 2 ;3. Look for a fast fall to 0 V and a curved rise toward 3.3 V.
TEXT 64 888 Left 2 ;If the plot is empty, select the schematic window and click the labeled wire again.
TEXT 64 968 Left 2 ;EXPERIMENTS AND COMMON QUESTIONS
TEXT 64 1008 Left 2 ;Right-click a component to edit its value. Predict first, change one value, then Run.
TEXT 64 1048 Left 2 ;TRY: Change CBUS from 200p to 400p; predict a slower rise.
TEXT 64 1088 Left 2 ;TRY: Change RPULLUP from 4.7k to 2.2k; predict a faster rise.
TEXT 64 1128 Left 2 ;FAQ: The pull-up charges CBUS after the switch releases the line.
TEXT 64 1168 Left 2 ;A smaller pull-up also increases current while the line is held low.
